    &\leq \int_{\Omega} \nu_\varrho(\mathrm{d} \eta) \, \Big|\mathbf E_{\eta}[f(Y^\tau_{t_1}(\varphi_1), \dots, Y^\tau_{t_n}(\varphi_n))] - \mathbf E_{Z_0^\tau(\eta)}^{\lim}[f(Y^{\lim}_{t_1}(\varphi_1), \dots, Y^{\lim}_{t_n}(\varphi_n))]\Big| \, ,
\end{equs}
and since we have already proved~\eqref{e:CVfindimQuenched}, we see that it only remains to show that, as $\tau \to \infty$, the process $Y_\cdot^{\lim}$ started from $Z_0^\tau$ (with $\eta \sim \nu_\varrho$) converges in law to the stationary process $\mathbf P_{\mathbb P}^{\lim}$ in $C(\mathbb{R}_+, \mathcal{S}'(\mathbb{R}^2))$. But this is a straightforward consequence of the convergence in law of $Z_0^\tau$ to $\mathbb P$, and the explicit representation~\eqref{e:YlimExplicit} for the process $Y^{\lim}_\cdot$. This concludes the proof.

