For conciseness, we denote $S_{t,\tau}^{(k)} := \sum_{x \in \mathbb{Z}^2} h_t^\tau(x)^{k} \, \sigma(x)^{k}$ for any $k \in \{1, \dots, n\}$. By comparing the two formulas~\eqref{e:ItauhMobius} and~\eqref{e:HermiteZ}, we deduce that, in order to prove~\eqref{e:CVchaosGoal2}, it only remains to show that, for any $\pi \in \Pi_n$, it holds
\begin{equ} \label{e:CVchaosGoal3}
